mod:store_rootless_destination;
// Landing 177d2b7, row 2 (DEF-643's new face, d643d): a store whose destination has no root name under its dereferences and casts -- a ternary, a `pick`,
// a `??`, a `??!` or a call under the dereference (`(<-(is (k > 0i64) : a : b)).lp = v`) -- lands its refs on the targets of the root's pointer value
// where one of them is the caller's storage: one of this function's own POINTER parameters, an Optional one's peeled, as `record_refs_at_target`
// separates them. Main recorded nothing for such a destination, so a callee's store through a selected parameter reached no summary, and the caller's
// view of what it replaced read freed heap. One site per face closed here, each a fault on main (78f9b3a):
//   DEF-643's eight (`e_pk`, `e_ter`, `e_ter1`, `e_ter2`, `g_ter1`, `s_opt`, `s_pk1`, `s_tc`); W2's attack on its own form (`a_bcall`, `a_bcall2`,
//   `a_call`, `a_cast`, `a_gen`, `a_gopt`, `a_lcp`, `a_loop`, `a_mix`, `a_nest`, `a_uopt`, `a_whole`, `a_wrap`); the W2 forms' attack (`c1lh`, `c1pa`,
//   `c1pp`, `c2e`, `c2h`, `c2m`, `s1_store`); W1's (`q_genp`, `q_ternp`); the W1 forms' attack (`b_rarm`, `b_rarmt`, `c4_optd`, `rel_ov`); the seats'
//   `y_opt2d` and `k_ex60` (`e_ter`'s selection under 60 casts).
// `k_ex70` is `e_ter`'s selection under 70 casts, past the walk's 64 steps: it is refused where the walk ends (BORROW-007), and the store, whose root
// the walk never reached, lands nothing, so the caller's growth adds no second report.
// Each cell's declarations carry its name as a suffix, and its `main` is `cell_main_<name>`. The controls that run are in
// tests/backend/programs/store_rootless_destination_ok.npk.
// PRICE: each cell marked PRICE below is a right program this row's text refuses, failing closed, at parity: its twin, the next cell, is refused by
// main (78f9b3a) at the same kind of site, for the same cause.
error:E5;
